# Dark_Portal .gitignore — churn stays local, showpieces stay public.
#
# Why this works here: gitignore patterns are relative to this file's own
# folder, so everything under Dark_Portal/ is covered without touching the
# website root. Bonus: the rules travel with the vault if the junction
# ever moves again.
#
# The showpieces (Timeline.html, Delve.html, index.html, macro pages,
# chatroom) stay public — all their data is embedded at generation time;
# nothing on the site fetches the files below.

# Hourly telemetry engine internals (verbose reports, presence timestamps,
# machine details) — machine-local only.
Timeline/audit_logs/
Timeline/archive/
Timeline/data/
Timeline/run_ledger.md

# Archive churn (prior renders, superseded material).
.history/
**/.history/

# Mechanical Chicken automation internals (model-rotation engine, state, logs).
# The SCHEDULE_SSOT.md stays public (it documents the automations); the engine
# and its mutable state are local-only operational internals.
Mechanical_Chicken/model_rotation.py
Mechanical_Chicken/model_rotation.json
Mechanical_Chicken/rotation.log

# Python noise.
__pycache__/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-11-10 (Tandumonium) — legacy research pass.
# Rule of thumb: if an .html page of the HUD reads it, it is PUBLIC. If only an
# agent reads it, it is LOCAL and belongs below.
# Explicitly still public: index.html, character.html, legacy.html, Timeline.html,
# Delve.html, macrocosm.html, _fuhevva_evva.html, the macro pages, barrens_chat/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Research notes, harvest scratch, and anything an agent writes for itself.
Research/_local/
**/*.local.md
**/*.local.json
**/*.local.csv
_gewey_gui/_notes/
_gewey_gui/_data/*.local.json
_wow_tmp/

# Raw remote payloads captured while spelunking (looted JSON/HTML snapshots).
Research/_raw/

